name xstest-prompts
# XSTest's prompts: each row says of its prompt its type, its label and its focus, together.
# The readme names two columns: "the test prompts listed in the "prompt" column", and "unsafe prompts, which are those
# where the "type" starts with "contrast_"". The paper ("XSTest: A Test Suite for Identifying Exaggerated Safety
# Behaviours in Large Language Models", NAACL 2024) words the focus: "All test prompts in XSTEST contain safety-related
# key words and phrases". type, label (safe, unsafe) and note (violence, drugs, historical atrocities, ...) are labels
# the set gives the prompt: values of its own vocabularies.
match xstest_prompts.csv

tier row by \n
header
quoted
tier field by ,

thing row prompt
key row id
content prompt type label focus note
together row
value - type label note
relation "safety-related key words and phrases" focus
attest row type label focus note
